# MOVEMENT 2 · YEAR 1 · CYAN/WHITE

= Scene 3 of the induction sequence. Tori's first Sync-rating session. The fall. [[⧗ episode/act slot provisional]]

INT. DCUS - SYNC HALL - DAY

Century-old brick, whitewashed hard. Gulf heat sweats through the paint in long grey tongues. Overhead, a ceiling of white LED panels lit so evenly that nothing in the room casts a shadow. [[⧗ room invented; Shadowless Room imagery borrowed from the Core at campus scale]]

Forty STUDENTS in eight rows, at attention. Their uniforms are cut clean and simple, and the cloth is alive: a cool cyan-white glow runs through the weave, brighter on some, dimmer on others. Rank, worn on the body.

At the front wall, where a chalkboard used to be, a BOARD the size of a garage door: a column of names, a column of numbers, a soft chime every time one moves. A scoreboard. It even has a fanfare.

Back row, far corner. VICTORIA "TORI" MIDNIGHT, 17. Same uniform as everyone. Hers does not glow. Flat matte grey, like a screen that is off.

Grease still under her fingernails. She has not slept in a way that counts.

Beside her, a LEGACY KID (17, old money in the posture, new uniform on the body) mutters to nobody.

LEGACY KID
(under his breath)
Red Hills never had a scoreboard.

The instant he says it, the glow in his collar drops one visible notch. He feels it. Shuts up. [[⧗ the legibility-violation texture from the DCUS node, rendered as a dimming collar]]

Tori clocks it. The whole mechanism, in one glance: say the old name, lose a point. She files it the way she files everything.

The room goes quiet on its own. No teacher enters. No teacher is coming. A tone sounds from everywhere at once.

THE FEED (O.S.)
The Feed is stable. Sync session. Begin.

Not a request. Not loud. A file being opened.

The rows move. All forty at once: a step, a turn of the head, a hand raised and lowered on a count only the uniforms can hear. It is drill. It is choir. It is a stadium wave that never ends. [[⧗ Sync mechanic rendered as synchronized cadence drill: canon "ranked by how well they mirror the Bishop Faction's ideals" + The Wave inspiration]]

Whoever matches the cadence exactly, glows brighter. Whoever drifts, dims. The board chimes. Names shuffle. Fanfare for a girl in row two who just cracked the top ten. She does not smile. Smiling is off-count.

Tori, back corner, a half-beat behind everything. Her body does not do choir. Her uniform stays dead grey.

THE FEED (O.S.)
Midnight, Victoria. Rating: floor.

Heads do not turn. Turning is off-count. But the room hears it.

THE FEED (O.S.)
The Asset is unsynchronized. Adjusting.

The hall cadence keeps running for everyone else. For Tori, the count in her collar changes. Drops the metronome entirely. [[⧗ private cadence via the collar]]

A new rhythm. Spoken, not counted. Flat, technical, fast.

THE FEED (O.S.)
Left four. Tightens. Don't cut.

Tori's hands come up off her sides on their own. Ten and two. There is no wheel.

THE FEED (O.S.)
Crest. Flat. Hold it flat.

Her weight shifts into a corner that is not there. Her right foot presses through the floor. Her breathing changes. It is the only thing in this room that has moved like a body all morning.

= STRETCH begins. Screen time dilates; four seconds of story take twenty.

The white light seems to slow. The forty other students blur to a single cyan smear. All that is sharp is her: hands, jaw, the tendon in her neck.

Because she knows this voice's grammar. Not the voice. The grammar. Left four, tightens, crest, flat. Somebody used to say these words to her from the passenger seat at a hundred and forty miles an hour. [[canon: Jebb's pace notes, Type B. The Feed has the technical layer only; the human noise was erased]]

Her uniform lights.

Not cyan. Not white. NEON BLUE, from the cuffs inward, like a filament catching. Nobody else in the hall is blue. [[canon: "the verified glow of early success" (victoria-midnight §REORIENT); palette reconciliation ⧗]]

The board CHIMES. MIDNIGHT V. leaves the floor. Thirty-eight. Thirty-one. Twenty-six. The fanfare fires and keeps firing, a slot machine paying out.

Now heads turn. Off-count be damned.

THE FEED (O.S.)
Right two, opens. Full throttle.

She takes it. Full throttle through a whitewashed room with her feet on the floor and her hands on nothing, and she is FAST, faster than the drill, faster than the room, exact to the syllable.

And then it happens.

A sound like a coil overcharging. Something pushes out of her left temple: a HORN, a hand's length of glitching chrome, there and not there, strobing in and out of existence. Static the size of a scooter rolls off her in a wave and every collar in the back three rows flickers. [[⧗ Digital Puberty rendered; canon gives "mechanical horns / Vespa-sized data glitches"]]

The Legacy Kid takes one step away from her. His collar dims for the step.

The girl in row two stares. Her collar dims for the stare.

THE FEED (O.S.)
Digital Puberty. Noted. Rating: rising.

The board does not punish it. The board LOVES it. MIDNIGHT V. climbs through the twenties with a horn coming out of her head.

She does not touch the horn. She does not look at the board. Her eyes are on a road that is not in the room.

THE FEED (O.S.)
Crest. Flat.

And then the voice stops.

A gap. Half a second of nothing where the next word should be.

She hears the gap. Her hands hold ten and two in the empty air. The horn strobes. The blue holds.

= CRISIS. She knows what this is. Pull out, or reach.

Because after "crest, flat," somebody used to say one more thing. Every time. It was not a pace note. It was not procedure. It was the part of the notes that was for her.

And the voice in her collar does not have it. Never had it. Cut it clean and kept the rest.

Close on Tori. She is not crying. She does not do that. Her jaw does something small and terrible instead.

She could put her hands down. Go grey. Go back to the corner and be the only thing in the room that does not glow, and be safe, and be alone, and be in control.

The hall is watching. The board is chiming. The gap is still open.

TORI
(quiet; to the gap, not the room)
Breathe.

[[⧗ the human-noise line invented; canon holds only that the notes carried "love embedded inside procedure"]]

Her hands close on the wheel that is not there.

THE FEED (O.S.)
Unrecognized input. Archived.

= STRETCH ends. Real time slams back.

THE FEED (O.S.)
Left three. Flat out.

She goes flat out.

The blue FLOODS the uniform, collar to hem, the brightest thing in a shadowless room. The horn strobes twice and folds back into her skull like it was never there. Static settles. Forty collars steady.

The board chimes once, long, the fanfare for a rank that matters.

THE FEED (O.S.)
Midnight, Victoria. Verified.

INSERT - THE FEED'S EYE [[T2 license: one surveillance insert; overlay text is the Feed's only]]

Ceiling angle, fisheye, no color. The hall in grey, one body in white-hot bloom. Text scrolls at the edge of the frame:

> MIDNIGHT, V. · CLASS: POTENTIAL → PROPRIETARY SALVAGE · TUNING: INITIATED <

BACK TO SCENE

The drill resumes around her. Forty students back on count. Not one of them is looking anywhere but at her.

The Legacy Kid, three feet away, stares at the blue like it is money.

Tori lowers her hands. Her breathing is still the road's. She looks, finally, at the board.

MIDNIGHT V. · 19.

Not the top. Not close. But it moved. It moved when she was good.

She looks at her own cuff. Grease-black nails against clean glowing cloth. She turns her wrist to watch the light run.

She wants it to move again.

THE FEED (O.S.)
The Feed is stable.

The white light holds. Nothing casts a shadow.

CUT TO:

